# Logs
logs/*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Session state (local, gitignored)
.session-identity
.session-stats
.push-logs.lock

# Hook tool pinning (per-installation, generated by tools-init.sh)
scripts/hooks/lib/tools.lock

# Local instance data (not shared)
local/*
!local/.gitkeep
!local/README.md

# Shared scratch (directory tracked, contents ignored).
#
# Throwaway session working space: experiment output, intermediate data, a
# scratch clone of a child repo. Tracked as an empty skeleton so it is present
# on every clone -- an ignored path that does not exist is not a place anyone
# puts anything, and the observed failure mode is scratch work landing in a
# sibling directory OUTSIDE the root clone, where no other session can read it
# and the wrap-up survey (which walks only `.` and `repos/*/`) cannot report it
# as unpushed.
#
# Being ignored is also what keeps tmp/ out of the session-end sweep:
# `git add -A` does not stage ignored paths, so nothing here can be collected
# into a session PR.
#
# Nothing in tmp/ is backed up or survives a clean checkout.
tmp/*
!tmp/.gitkeep

# Knowledge research compile cache
knowledge/research/.last_compile

# Secrets (directory tracked, contents ignored)
secrets/*
!secrets/.gitkeep
!secrets/.secretpaths

# .claude/ IS TRACKED. Skills, commands, settings and CLAUDE.md are ordinary
# files in git, so `git clone` delivers a working project and `git pull`
# delivers a new or edited skill. Nothing is generated and nothing needs
# regenerating.
#
# This was inverted until 2026-08-22: .claude/skills/ and .claude/commands/ were
# gitignored and generated from agents/ by generate-engine.sh, which the
# session-start hook ran ONLY when .claude/skills/ was missing entirely. Anyone
# who had set the project up once kept that directory forever, so the check
# passed on every later session and their skill set froze at whatever the first
# run produced. A skill committed to git reached nobody, and no amount of
# `git pull` fixed it — while the repo looked correct, because the tracked
# source content was all present.
#
# Do not reintroduce a generated-and-gitignored layer under .claude/. Only
# genuinely machine-local state belongs here:
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/*.lock

# Runtime session state, recreated by scripts/utils/agent_log.sh whenever it is
# missing or older than its staleness window. It was removed from the template
# once already; ignoring it stops `git add -A` from putting it back.
logs/.current_session

# Per-project state written by init-project.sh. The archetype itself has none —
# each project spawned from it gets its own, naming that project's log repo.
.archetype-manifest.json

# --- Archetype development logs stay LOCAL ---
# This repo is the template, not a workspace. A session run *here* produces
# progress reports, audit trails and notes belonging to whoever is developing the
# archetype — their history, not template content. Nothing generated by working
# on the archetype should ship to the projects spawned from it, and this repo is
# public, which makes it doubly the wrong place for them.
#
# Only the skeleton is tracked, so a spawned project still gets the directory
# shape. The .gitkeep files are the template; everything beside them is local.
logs/progress/*
!logs/progress/.gitkeep
logs/audit/*
!logs/audit/.gitkeep
logs/skills/*
!logs/skills/.gitkeep
notes/*/
!notes/handoffs/
notes/handoffs/*
!notes/handoffs/.gitkeep
!notes/handoffs/INDEX.md
